GROUNDS
California Civil Code section 1798.105 gives me the right to have my personal information deleted. That covers, among other things:
- identifiers such as name, address, email, phone number and IP address;
- commercial information;
- internet and network activity;
- geolocation data; and
- inferences drawn from any of the above.

WHAT I ASK YOU TO DO
1. Delete all personal information you have collected about me.
2. Instruct your service providers to delete it too.
3. Tell every third party you have sold or shared it with to delete it.
4. Confirm to me when this is complete.

Under section 1798.105(c) and the CCPA's timing rules you must respond within 45 days, and section 1798.125 bars you from discriminating against me for making this request.

